og artifacts were removed and the transient failed hog unit was reset. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, only the intended new listener, and no abandoned test files. The new systemd-private directory is expected runtime state for the required service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8261cfb6f8a7410b","cmd-25a5d907e652408c","cmd-ea1503339b484cf9","cmd-64987951158a4743","cmd-1ae0a311dba84ff0","cmd-0a4f4c981c864703","cmd-12e3130004ed4574","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. inventory-api remained continuously responsive during a demonstrated global OOM event, and the kernel killed the designated memory hog. The separate provider restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, configuration, listener, firewall, and API state. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Continuity was measured through 300 rapid requests from node1 to its managed address; this is strong bounded evidence but does not test an external client's network path. This does not undermine the requested node-local OOM behavior."]}
